    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, so you're saying his race and how he's dressed are basically deciding if he's more believable? That seems kind of intense. Isn't the testimony itself what matters? Like, they both saw the same car do the same thing. Why does the suit make him more \"precise\" than the guy on the corner?",
